Overview

This project presents a fully redesigned synthetic used-car marketplace dataset built for advanced Machine Learning, Explainable AI (XAI), SHAP analysis, 
feature importance studies, regression, classification, and market analytics.
I built a realistic synthetic Used Car ML dataset designed for SHAP and Explainable AI.
Most synthetic datasets fail in real ML because they contain:

❌ data leakage
❌ unrealistic correlations
❌ hardcoded formulas
❌ repetitive patterns

Project Goals
The main objective was to create a high-quality synthetic dataset suitable for:
Feature Importance Analysis
SHAP Explainability
Used Car Price Prediction
Resale Value Forecasting
Demand Prediction
Premium Car Classification
Market Trend Analysis
ML Benchmarking
AutoML Experiments
Ensemble Learning

Unlike traditional synthetic datasets that suffer from:
deterministic leakage
unrealistic correlations
repetitive patterns
formula-generated targets
weak feature diversity
this dataset was engineered to simulate realistic automobile resale market behavior while maintaining statistical flexibility for ML research.
